<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Drysdale and Clifton Springs sit on the northern Bellarine, and a lot of the housing here went up while asbestos cement was ordinary building material. It was standard in Australian homes from the mid-1940s until the late 1980s, and the national estimate is that it is still present in one in three homes. If your place was built or extended before 1990, the back fence, the garage roof, the eaves lining and the sheet behind the bathroom tiles are all worth a second look before anyone puts a tool through them.</p><p>Barwon Asbestos Co is not a removal company and holds no licence. What we do is get the material identified and put you in touch with licensed asbestos removalists working across the Bellarine, and their WorkSafe Victoria licence number appears on the quote you receive. You deal with them directly. Call 0480 XXX XXX, or send a photo of what you are looking at and we will point you to the sensible first step, which is usually <a href="/asbestos-testing-geelong/">a test</a> rather than a removal quote.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Drysdale & Clifton Springs</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Drysdale & Clifton Springs Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos Testing and Identification</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Nobody can tell fibro from plain cement sheet by eye, and a builder or a pest inspector cannot either, so <a href="/asbestos-testing-geelong/">a sample goes to a NATA accredited laboratory</a>. Published Victorian rates run $88 to $160 per sample, and most houses need three to eight samples, because a fence, an eaves lining and a bathroom sheet count as three different materials.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos Fence Removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Old fibro boundary fences are the job we hear about most from Drysdale and Clifton Springs, and a cracked or crumbling sheet matters far more than an intact one. Published Victorian <a href="/asbestos-fence-removal-geelong/">whole fence jobs</a> run $1,000 to $3,500, and a full boundary line is well past anything that can be taken on unlicensed.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos Roof and Shed Removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Super Six roofing on garages, sheds and the odd farm outbuilding on the land behind Drysdale is the higher risk work, because the sheets are brittle and the first instinct is usually to water blast them. Published Victorian <a href="/asbestos-roof-removal-geelong/">roof removal</a> runs $40 to $120 per square metre, with a garage or small roof at $3,500 to $5,500.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos Disposal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Drysdale Landfill is the one site in the Barwon region on EPA Victoria's register of landfills licensed to receive asbestos, and it takes small domestic quantities only, capped at a 6 by 4 trailer load. Fees apply, the council does not publish the asbestos figure, and you need to ring (03) 5251 2935 before you turn up with a <a href="/asbestos-disposal-geelong/">wrapped and labelled load</a>.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
